close_reason: "Budget compaction exempts only the envelope's continuation tokens, so a budgeted list whose item carries an oversized cursor-named field returns its compacted row again"
contract_change:
  api: "Read-output string compaction on get, list and search (budgeted reads, with or without --for)"
  before: "Since 2026.11.12 every string under a key named cursor or ending in _cursor stayed whole at any depth, including an item field such as a custom sync_cursor, so a budgeted list could omit its rows"
  after: "Only the envelope and non-item surfaces keep that exemption; the fields of item and of every items row compact like other content, as before 2026.11.12"
  migrate: "To read an item field named like a cursor in full, repeat the read with --output-budget unbounded (outputBudget: \"unbounded\"); continuation tokens in the envelope are unchanged"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_strengthened
